			"date": "2022-12-16T20:13:15.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> Reader enabled a decentralized ecosystem and it's demise pushed us into more centralised publishing and identity (Twitter, FB, IG, etc). I feel like this is almost an opposite moment. It's showing many people who were resistant before why the convenience of centralization brings costs that may be too great.</p>",
